s.more("engm-la-cayley", sections=[dict(h="Diagonalisation step by step", md="""1. Find the eigenvalues λ₁, …, λₙ.
2. For each, find a basis of the eigenspace from (A − λI)x = 0.
3. If there are n independent eigenvectors, put them as the columns of P; then P⁻¹AP = D = diag(λ₁, …, λₙ).
4. Powers become easy: Aᵏ = PDᵏP⁻¹, so Aᵏ has eigenvalues λᵏ.

Distinct eigenvalues guarantee step 3. Real symmetric matrices are always diagonalisable, even with repeated eigenvalues, and P can be chosen orthogonal.""")])
s.more("engm-pb-distributions", sections=[dict(h="Which distribution?", md="""| The story | Distribution |
|---|---|
| number of successes in a fixed number n of independent trials | Binomial(n, p) |
| number of trials until the first success | Geometric(p) |
| number of rare events in a fixed interval, average rate λ | Poisson(λ) |
| one trial, success or failure | Bernoulli(p) |

When n is large and p small, Binomial(n, p) ≈ Poisson(np).""")])
